1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,420
Good morning. I'm very pleased to have been invited along to your club to talk about our Charity Sponsored Walking Holiday for Education Aid.

2
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:12,510
I'll start by giving you a brief overview of what it entails.

3
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:16,440
First of all let me explain what we mean by 'sponsored' here.

4
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:20,040
This is where people promise to donate money to the charity

5
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:21,338
if you achieve your goal,

6
00:00:21,338 --> 00:00:24,400
in this case to walk a certain number of miles.

7
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:28,160
Basically we are organizing a ten-day holiday

8
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,796
from the sixth to the sixteenth of November,

9
00:00:30,796 --> 00:00:35,060
with eight days actual walking, trekking in the Semira Mountains.

10
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:38,280
Let's have a look at some of the details.

11
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:43,444
We require you to raise sponsorship money of at least $3,200,

12
00:00:43,444 --> 00:00:50,760
paying $250 of it up front as a deposit and the rest in stages throughout the year.

13
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:55,255
Out of this about thirty-five per cent will go on your expenses,

14
00:00:55,255 --> 00:00:59,750
and that leaves sixty-five per cent guaranteed to go to the charity.

15
00:00:59,750 --> 00:01:02,840
Which brings me to the most important part.

16
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:08,200
This trek is being specifically organized to help education in the Semira region.

17
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:11,640
Last year we helped train teachers for the disabled

18
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:14,560
and this year we're focusing on the pupils.

19
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:22,230
Each of the walkers' sponsorship money will go to help an individual special needs pupil in one of the mountain schools.

20
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:26,520
In the second part of the talk I'll be giving you a lot more details

21
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,880
but back to the basic information.

22
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:34,809
Age limits. This is the second time we have run this kind of holiday and um,

23
00:01:34,809 --> 00:01:38,160
on the first we even had an eighty-year old

24
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:42,220
but we found it was wise to establish limits this time.

25
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:46,639
You have to be at least eighteen and the top limit is now seventy,

26
00:01:46,639 --> 00:01:50,340
though you need to obtain a health certificate from your doctor

27
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:52,320
if you are over sixty years old.

28
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:56,760
Now, the Semira Mountains are among the highest in the world

29
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,185
but you mustn't be too daunted,

30
00:01:58,185 --> 00:02:01,290
we will mainly be trekking in the foothills only,

31
00:02:01,290 --> 00:02:04,740
although there will be spectacular views even in the foothills.

32
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:08,560
However, you will need to be extremely fit

33
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:11,270
if you aren't now and you're interested in coming with us.

34
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:13,740
You have plenty of time to get into shape.

35
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:15,778
You will be sleeping in tents

36
00:02:15,778 --> 00:02:19,660
so you must have quite a bit of equipment with you

37
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:22,230
but you will be helped by local assistants.

38
00:02:22,230 --> 00:02:25,120
Your bedding and so forth will be carried by them.

39
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:29,820
We ask that you only walk with a small rucksack with needs for the day.

40
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:35,060
I don't think I've really said enough about the marvellous area you'll be walking in.

41
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:37,970
Let's have a look at some of the sights you'll be seeing.

42
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:42,240
Apart from these spectacular snow-covered peaks and valleys

43
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:44,820
there are marvellous historic villages.

44
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:48,573
The area has been famous for centuries for making beautiful carpets,

45
00:02:48,573 --> 00:02:53,690
although recently there has been a trend to move into weaving blankets and wood carving.

46
00:02:53,690 --> 00:02:56,750
The people are extremely friendly and welcoming.

47
00:02:56,750 --> 00:03:02,960
We deliberately keep the parties small in size to minimize disruption to people and landscape.

48
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:05,570
I hope that there are still some people interested.

49
00:03:05,570 --> 00:03:10,549
I will be distributing leaflets at the end where you can find out more information,

50
00:03:10,549 --> 00:03:14,040
but just for the moment I'll outline the itinerary

51
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,860
the main high points of the holiday.

52
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:21,000
Obviously, you'll start by flying out to Kishba, the capital city, on Day One.

53
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,648
After a couple of days to acclimatize yourself,

54
00:03:23,648 --> 00:03:27,952
you'll start the trek on Day Three walking through the enormous Katiba Forest

55
00:03:27,952 --> 00:03:30,600
which will take the whole of the day.

56
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,570
Day Four takes us higher up,

57
00:03:32,570 --> 00:03:35,540
going through the foothills past a number of villages

58
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:38,480
and visiting a school for the disabled in Sohan.

59
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:41,800
Then you have a rest day, that's Day Five

60
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,779
before going to the spectacular Kumi Temple

61
00:03:44,779 --> 00:03:49,760
with twelfth-century carvings, set in a small forest by a lake

62
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:52,260
and that's Day Six, the highlight for many.

63
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:57,239
We stay near there for Day Seven because then comes the hardest day,

64
00:03:57,239 --> 00:03:59,660
walking through very mountainous country

65
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:02,600
but culminating in a swim in the Parteh Falls.

66
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:06,584
This is the highest waterfall in the region. Day Nine is much easier,

67
00:04:06,584 --> 00:04:09,680
with part of the day spent in a village

68
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:12,100
where they make some of the gorgeous red blankets.

69
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:15,540
Then back down to Kishba and the journey home.

70
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:19,550
So you can see it's a pretty packed timetable...
